<title>USA: Cross-Continent Auto vice chairman resigns.</title>
<headline>Cross-Continent Auto vice chairman resigns.</headline>
<dateline>AMARILLO, Texas 1997-03-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Cross-Continent Auto Retailers Inc said on Monday its vice chairman, Ezra Mager, resigned to pursue other opportunities.</p>
<p>James Purser, the company's chief financial officer, will be appointed to the board in Mager's place, the company said.</p>
<p>Cross-Continent owns and operates 10 franchised auto dealerships in Colorado, Nevada, Oklahoma and Texas.</p>
